Il giorno , Michael Turniansky <mturniansky@gmail.com> ha scritto:
> Should we insist on .i separators in the second and subsequent panels?

I think we should. I always envisaged lojban comics dialags to be a  
continous stream of text for each character speaking.

One might think that there's an implicit {.i} at the begininng of a new  
balloon but this would break some dialogue that uses multiple balloons for  
a single utterance (for example to show a different point of view in a new  
panel).

I once experimented with using ":" as an alternative ortography for {.i}  
(just imagine the initial dot and the small dot over the "i" to be  
re-arranged in space) but it doesn't seem to have caught on. There's an  
example here:  
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-download_wiki_attachment.php?attId=751 .

